  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_019 (multimodal, multiprofile, PCA, ResNet50, avgpool, weighted) at 0.639 acc. Key findings: multiprofile > single (+0.106 for RNA), weighted > concat fusion (+0.020), avgpool > transformer aggregation (+0.040), and image contributes modestly (+0.028 over RNA alone). The RNA encoder has only been tested as PCA (linear, 2000-dim); scVI and scGPT are completely unexplored. Since RNA is the dominant modality (0.591 alone vs 0.208 for image), the quality of the RNA representation is likely the highest-leverage untested design choice. Question: Does a learned nonlinear encoder (scVI) improve over linear PCA in the best-performing multimodal setup? This experiment changes only the RNA encoder from PCA to scVI while holding all other settings (multiprofile, ResNet50, avgpool, weighted) at their empirically best values, cleanly isolating the encoder effect. Why this is the best next experiment: It tests the single most impactful unexplored axis (RNA representation) in the current best configuration, providing a direct comparison that will tell us whether investing in richer RNA encoders is worthwhile before exploring image encoder upgrades or other combinations."
}

